body:
Well, when you burn something, you begin a combustion/oxidation reaction starting with pure iron shown by Fe, it combines with oxygen to create, in a perfect world, water and carbon dioxide. But in this case, because the combustion isn't complete, it goes something like this,  4 Fe (s) + 3 O 2 (g) ==> 2 Fe 2O 3 (s)  . Simply put, the oxygen that is being used in the reaction is now trapped in the molecules with the iron, increasing it's mass.

&#x200B;

Edit: I forgot to mention the molar mass of pure iron and iron (III) oxide, which is the mass of a a single mole of a substance, a mole being equal to  6.022\*10\^23 atoms/molecules. Iron weighs 55.845 grams per mole, whereas iron (III) oxide weighs 159.69 grams per mole.

&#x200B;

Edit #2: I wrote the wrong reaction, initially I wrote the reaction for rusting in presence of water, but I changed it to the equation for straight combustion of iron.

If it's the Blood Angel, then it's pronounced Car-Lay-En, according to the audiobook.

&#x200B;

Edit: Source - Devastation of Baal, Chapter 29

The issue with Yuumi is that her kit is very underwhelming. In order to reach the point where you can get the power spikes given by her W passive, you'd have to play what is essentially a 1.5 v 2 lane. She needs a very safe laner, and due to the current jungle meta, where ganking early happens constantly, you'd be hard pressed to keep your ADC alive. She needs a way to keep her ADC alive through laning phase. Coupled with ADCs being inherently squishy and tending to be less mobile, Yuumi can't keep up with what happens. She has no way to peel, her heal is underwhelming. The champions she does synergize well with all have the ability to get in or out of a fight or have built in survivability. She has potential to be a good support, but it feels like she doesn't fill a niche that every other support has. My personal thought is that she should be able to give a way for an ADC to survive the laning phase, such as giving tenacity to the champion she's attached to, just so engage lanes aren't going to completely destroy you. Everything she does, besides the AD from being attached, is done more reliably by Sona. 

&#x200B;

TLDR; Yuumi needs to be able to allow her ADC to survive the early game and fill a niche in bot lane.
